<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_TheRot                                     UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-09
    BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1. Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_rot.md
    (FROZEN). Replaces the donor `AB_MycoticJungle` (Alpha Biomes' "Mycotic
    Jungle"). Sheet-named "THE ROT" (owner's pick).

    MEASURED live on V25 (sheet SS0, post cold-tail repaint 2026-09-08): 2,258 tiles,
    arc 74-135, temp p10/median/p90 -35.5/-18.8/+12.9 C.

    Weather LEFT AT DONOR VALUES, deliberately: ban 3 reads "No water rain (R-H1) —
    the Sheen is emission; a water-rain weather def here is a violation," but SS4b
    is explicit that this is a RESKIN, not a removal — "Sheen-fall (re-skin of the
    donor's 'very common rains')." The donor's Rain/RainyThunderstorm/FoggyRain
    commonalities ARE the Sheen mechanically; renaming the WeatherDefs themselves is
    separate, un-owed content (no bespoke WeatherDef exists yet). Kept as-is rather
    than zeroed, which would have silently deleted the Sheen instead of reskinning
    it.

    diseaseMtbDays/animalDensity/plantDensity(plant density trimmed from donor's 0.2
    — see below) match the donor's read-in values (sheet SS0 "Donor inventory taken
    in"). plantDensity: donor dump showed 0.2; kept close (0.6 chosen mid-range, see
    Owed) is NOT grounded in a sheet number — flagged: the sheet gives no explicit
    plantDensity figure, and "dense beyond anything dayside... this is the
    nightside's lush" (SS2) argues for HIGH density on a fungal-jungle read. Left at
    an interim value pending a quicktest tune, same pattern RUT_TheScald/RUT_GreySea
    used for their animalDensity.

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml against rosters/the_rot.json. Ban 1 (no conventional
    plants) and ban 2 (no pure-animal residents, hybrid-or-out) are roster-level
    bans already enforced by that JSON.

    NOT this pass's scope: the heat-generating gene (still unauthored, SS Owed); the
    live-tea/symbiont mechanics (storage ban 4); the pale-tree anima reskin.

    UPDATE (FUNGALFOREST_RAID_MERGE_1, offline half, this pass): the wildPlants list
    below now points at our own `RUT_`-prefixed flora
    (`src/RimUtinni/RotSporeKit/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RUT_RotSporeKit_Flora.xml`)
    instead of the donor's `BMT_`-prefixed defs, per the ingestion ruling in
    `the_rot.md` §7b. wildAnimals is UNCHANGED (still donor `BMT_`/`AA_` defNames,
    MayRequire'd) — fauna admission is a separate sitting,
    `BIOME_FAUNA_ASSIGNMENT_SITTING_1`. The 425-tile `BMT_FungalForest` -> biome-merge
    repaint itself (the other half of that item) has NOT happened yet — still owed,
    gated on the owner reviewing the offline render this pass produced.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_TheRot</defName>
    <label>the Rot</label>
    <description>A pale fungal continent on the night shoulder of the stormwall: bone-white and lilac towers under a black sky, a glow-moss floor warm to lie on while the air above it would kill you, milky ponds that are not water. Nothing here is a plant. Nothing here is quite an animal. Everything is connected, everything is warm from the inside, and everything -- including what you take away with you -- is still alive.</description>
    <workerClass>AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_MycoticJungle</workerClass>
    <foragedFood>RawFungus</foragedFood>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.9</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.6</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.5</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/AB_MycoticJungle</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>35</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">
        <diseaseInc>AB_Disease_SporesAllergy</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">
        <diseaseInc>AB_Disease_AnimalSporesAllergy</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
